b-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1408,"digest":"sha256:5c4643108438c42eb24d9b76f7815b96479939d3be1fc59cd7dc779fb6bc5cb7","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-08T09:18:12Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T09:18:13Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/catethos/Aphid/releases/download/v0.1.0-dev/x86_64-linux-gnu-identity.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catethos/Aphid/tarball/v0.1.0-dev","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catethos/Aphid/zipball/v0.1.0-dev","body":"# Aphid v0.1.0-dev — experimental native validation prerelease\n\nNo target is release-supported and no implementation stage is complete. Aphid\nis not published to Hex. This prerelease contains native validation archives,\nidentity/audit records, checksums and retained third-party notice files; it\ncontains no bundled ERTS release.\n\n| Native archive | SHA256 |\n|---|---|\n| `aphid-0.1.0-dev-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz` | `fa9535c7e8f3b149658ed0f5f98329f7142cfd21f30f20fef765c74c42b798cc` |\n| `aphid-0.1.0-dev-aarch64-linux-gnu.tar.gz` | `235ceb0490a1baf64e33fd53f17f683ce263197cf0cac6cf1107275dd94b62af` |\n| `runtime-validation-aarch64-macos-13.3-baseline-3.tar.gz` | `3125907a738162c55ba8f68874c861c767bc7a5f17e9b23c69f028df192e3034` |\n\nNative Linux qualification: run `34193449987`. Refreshed source qualification:\nrun `34205212486`. One exact source package with SHA256\n`11ca5ca447a7a93ee6d8e2d79758f3ed67d9ce04d20947a08e82598851152507`\npassed 92 tests on native Linux x86_64/ARM64 and macOS ARM64 with fresh caches,\nnormal locked Hex dependency acquisition, denied native compiler/development-tree\naccess, and unchanged native hashes. That Hex source archive is not an attached\nasset and is not GitHub's automatic source snapshot.\n\nLinux ephemeral bundled-ERTS validation releases passed startup/restart,\noffline shutdown/persistent reopen and startup failure checks. They are not\nattached. The latest macOS qualification is a consumer proof; earlier macOS\nbundled-ERTS evidence applies only to its original source package.\n\n`SHA256SUMS` covers the eight Linux/notice payloads; `SHA256SUMS-macos` covers the\nthree macOS payloads. The source package installs the supplemental notice file\nbeside the native archive's license tree. The supplement's SHA256 is\n`08cc1d20ccb4808537545220152d6aff97701e2c3b0b8597ab2dadaa82a789d1`.\nThe standalone notice attachment is not automatically fetched by native consumers.\nThe archived applications contain Aphid and Telemetry modules, with no bundled\nPegasus, ZigParser or NimbleParsec modules and no ERTS. Those parser packages are\nbuild dependencies acquired separately. The retained native component map's\nnotice texts are present in the archive license trees plus the supplement.\nBroader build provenance and production-runtime review remain follow-up work;\nthis is not an exhaustive attribution certification.\n\nExecution is proved only on Ubuntu 24.04/glibc 2.39 and macOS 26.6, using Elixir\n1.20.0 / OTP 29.0.4. Linux installation requires GNU objcopy; macOS requires\notool. The Linux engine requires GLIBC 2.38 and GLIBCXX 3.4.32. macOS native\ncommands declare 13.3; neither those declarations nor ELF requirements prove\nminimum-system/CPU execution. Other OTP/binutils, x86_64-to-ARM64 cross-build,\nfresh source installation and remaining implementation gates are unproved.\nDuckDB stays 1.4.4.\n\nThe fixed tag's catalog URLs remain disabled. Public availability alone does not\nprove package-default installation. A separately reviewed URL-enabled source\npackage must pass fresh consumers against the actual repository endpoint on all\nthree native targets. No silent source fallback or Hex publication is enabled.\n\n## Notices accompanying direct archive downloads\n\nKeep `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` and these release notices with the downloaded native\narchive, alongside its `licenses/` directory. The installer uses the supplement\nfrom its source package; a direct archive download does not fetch that attachment.\nThe unchanged macOS validation archive omits the Zig notice included below;\nthe Linux archives already contain the same text. Zigler's notice is also\npreserved in the supplement under the content-matched ZigGet parent license.\n\n### Zig 0.16.0 runtime and standard-library notice\n\nThe MIT License (Expat)\n\nCopyright (c) Zig contributors\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in\nall copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN\nTHE SOFTWARE.\n"}